Five working diagrams of how this project fits together, straight from the project's own planning docs, unedited. Colors are the same CityLink yellow, purple, and cream the site itself uses, pulled from the bus's own livery.

**How someone becomes a member**, from application through to active (or not).

<img src="/diagrams/launch-member-v0/member-lifecycle.svg" alt="Member lifecycle: submit application, verify email, keyholder claims and tours, one keyholder decides, then assent leads to active, paused, left, or removed." />

**What happens after you're active.** Contributions and other extras stay optional, and separate from membership itself.

<img src="/diagrams/launch-member-v0/member-projection-flow.svg" alt="Member projection flow: active membership branches into an optional contribution offer (zero, cash or check, or Stripe) and an optional projection queue for mailing list and mailbox, none of which change membership." />

**How a tool moves** from the shelf to your hands and back.

<img src="/diagrams/launch-member-v0/inventory-custody-flow.svg" alt="Inventory custody flow: scan a tool, check its availability and condition, finalize a loan, then scan it back in, inspect it, and route it to available or quarantine." />

**How the pieces of the system talk to each other**, in plain shapes.

<img src="/diagrams/launch-member-v0/launch-authority-flow.svg" alt="Launch authority flow: visitors reach the public site and a join link into the member app, both built from private source into images served by the project's own infrastructure." />

**How a change gets checked and proven** before it ever reaches the live site.

<img src="/diagrams/launch-member-v0/release-proof-flow.svg" alt="Release proof flow: a ready issue becomes a branch and a proposed change, passes review and human QA, gets a human ship decision, then moves through pinned, running, and served proof, with rollback if anything fails." />
